1439:
Historic properties or landmarks may be buildings, structures, sites, or objects including the adjacent area necessary for the proper appreciation or use thereof, deemed worthy of preservation by reason of value to the United States, the state of Georgia, Newton County, or the city, for one of the following reasons:
A. It is an outstanding example of a structure representative of its era;
B. It is one of few remaining examples of a past architectural style;
C. It is a place or structure associated with an event or person of historic or cultural significance to the city, Newton County, the state of Georgia, or the region; or
D. It is a site of natural or aesthetic interest that is continuing to contribute to the cultural or historical development and heritage of the city, Newton County, the state of Georgia or the region.
(Ord. dated 6/30/08 (part))

1441:
